30,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I have learned that our county grants only cover session fees for the first year, and that winter road closures north of the river happened eleven days last year, though community halls remained open.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It appears we have a significant accessibility gap. Residents in two outer wards now face an hour's round trip to reach us due to lost bus links, and our physical hours don't match peak remote usage.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that people really loved the outreach stops in the outer wards! But also, a digitisation project from six years ago was a bit of a mess because half the images weren't indexed.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our financial patterns are as predictable as they are precarious. We have a tendency to overrun vehicle costs while letting equipment funds slip back into reserves, and our grants are merely temporary bridges.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Regarding our capacity, we have skilled volunteers for repairs, but we lack staff trained to supervise outside facilitators. Furthermore, we no longer have a technician to keep power tools certified.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is concerning that our grants are so short-lived. We must be careful not to start something we cannot sustain once that first year passes, lest we disappoint the community.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I agree. Given the lost bus links, we must consider how to reach those who can no longer reach us. A service that brings the library to them would address this gap.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"That's a great idea, @Jonathan! My papers showed that people in the outer wards really loved the outreach stops. We should definitely do something that goes to them!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While the sentiment is noble, @Jonathan, we must consider the ledger. Our vehicle running costs already overran by a third last year. A mobile service might be a financial leak we cannot afford to ignore.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"If we consider a workshop, we must also face the fact that we have no one on staff to certify power tools or supervise facilitators. We cannot simply rely on volunteers for safety and oversight.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, you make a very fair point about the costs. However, if the community halls are still accessible during winter, perhaps there is a way to reach people without relying solely on our own vehicles.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that is a thoughtful observation. If we can utilize existing community spaces, we might mitigate some risks, though the primary issue remains the lack of transport for residents to reach any staffed counter.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But we can't just forget about the people who can't get here! If the outreach stops were so popular before, maybe we can find a way to make them work again without breaking the bank!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, your passion is admirable, but passion rarely balances a ledger. If we ignore the pattern of overspending on vehicles, we are simply scheduling a future crisis. We need a sustainable structure, not a temporary triumph.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I agree that sustainability is key. However, we must also consider that any program requiring specialized supervision or technical certification is currently unfeasible without new staff training or hires. We cannot ignore the skill gap.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we are all very concerned with sustainability, whether it be financial, technical, or logistical. Perhaps we should look for a path that serves the most people without creating a burden we cannot carry.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Shizue. We must balance the urgent need for accessibility in the outer wards with the financial and staffing constraints Benjamin and Minako have highlighted. We need a solution that is both inclusive and sustainable.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I just want us to pick something that actually works! If the old evening groups are still meeting on their own, maybe we should do something like that? Something that lasts!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, you've hit upon a vital point. The success of those independent groups suggests that the most sustainable services are those that empower the community rather than those that create a permanent, expensive dependency on our fleet.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"Exactly. If we choose a path that leverages existing community strengths rather than creating new, unmanageable overhead for our staff, we ensure the service actually survives. We must avoid any proposal that requires certifications we cannot provide.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
