59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at our options, the Language Learning Circles seem most promising. They utilize partner organizations and facilitators, which avoids the vehicle costs Benjamin fears and the certification issues Minako mentioned. It feels like a gentle, sustainable way to grow.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Shizue. The Language Learning Circles can be hosted in those community halls, bridging the accessibility gap for the outer wards without the financial risk of a mobile fleet or the staffing burdens of a workshop.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,I like the Language Learning Circles too! It's like those evening groups I found that are still going. It sounds like something that will actually last and not just be a mess!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The logic is sound. The Language Learning Circles avoid the vehicle budget trap and the certification void, while leveraging the community's own resilience. It is a rare instance where the most compassionate choice is also the most rational.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree. The Language Learning Circles rely on partner organizations and facilitators, which avoids the supervision and certification gaps I identified. It is the only option that is both operationally feasible and sustainable for our current staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,It is such a relief to see us all in agreement. It feels as though we have found a path that respects both our limitations and our hopes for the community. Shall we proceed to the vote?,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. The Language Learning Circles address the needs of our residents while remaining within our means. I am ready to cast my vote.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,Me too! I'm so happy we all agree! Let's do the Language Learning Circles! I'm ready to vote!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Since we have reached a consensus based on both the financial data and the operational constraints, I see no reason to delay. I am ready to vote for the Language Learning Circles.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,I agree. The evidence clearly points to this as the most viable option. I am ready to vote for the Language Learning Circles.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I shall cast my vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is a wonderful way to bring people together while ensuring we can keep our promise to them for years to come.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I cast my vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is the most inclusive choice that respects our current logistical constraints and ensures accessibility for all.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I vote for the Language Learning Circles! It's the best one and I'm so glad we all like it!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I cast my vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is the only proposal that satisfies our fiscal caution and operational reality while still providing a meaningful service to the public.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,I cast my vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is the only proposal that aligns with our staffing capabilities and ensures long-term operational stability.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
